COMPILING AND RUNNING 

ASSUMPTIONS:
The code will not create or insert starting data. To do this, please use the provided code found in Database.sql to create the table and insert data through pgAdmin4.  
To connect to the database, the code will ask for the database name and the password to your account. 

TO RUN: 
1. This program requires that psycopg2 be installed. If this has already been downloaded, skip the next step. 
2. To install psychopg2, open the terminal either in the IDE or open command prompt. Once in the termainal, run "python -m pip install psycopg2"
    Note: I had to use "py" instead of "python"
3. Once psychopg2 has been downloaded, navigate to the directory containing the provided code. 
4. Now in the desired directory, in the terminal, enter "python question1.py" (Note: for me again, I have to use "py" instead of "python")
5. The code will ask for you to enter your database name and the password to your account. It will connect to the database before printing out the different CRUD operations. 
Enter the number of the operation and follow the next steps if provided. 

